# C# sources are checked out with LF on every OS. Tests build MIME messages and mail headers from multi-line raw string
# literals; with Git for Windows' default (core.autocrlf=true) those literals became CRLF and four tests failed on
# Windows only (Windows prerelease run 45681061181) although the app itself reads mail as raw bytes from the network.
*.cs text eol=lf
# Mail fixtures are byte-exact RFC 5322 messages (CRLF): never converted.
*.eml -text
